<ontology/use_leather_tanning/use_leather_tanning__0132__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1612" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n1612> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Valonia used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1612"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "VALONIA: A species of acorn, forming a very considerable article of export from the Morea and the Levant. The more substance there is in the husk, or cup of the acorn, the better. It is of a bright drab colour, which it preserves so long as it is kept dry; any dampness injures it; as it then turns black, and loses both its strength and value. It is principal..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
